{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14307 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "Chlorothiazide is linked to Ataxin-2 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of cellular processes. The evidence suggests that chlorothiazide acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[...]-oxane-3,4,5-triol and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[...]-phenol. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of Ataxin-2, indicating a potential pathway where chlorothiazide indirectly influences Ataxin-2 through Caspase-5. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ataxin-2 suggests a complex regulatory network, possibly involving caspase-mediated signaling. The integration of these findings highlights the role of Caspase-5 as a central mediator in the interaction between chlorothiazide and Ataxin-2, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
